{"OptimizedImage.downsize is defined twice; the later definition overrides the earlier and changes the method arity, causing existing callers (e.g., ResizeEmoji) to raise ArgumentError at runtime": 0.924113929271698, "API URL uploads now download up to a hardcoded 10MB, ignoring SiteSettings and causing inconsistent behavior with server-side validation": 0.944246768951416, "The downloader loop can exceed the requested cap by up to one chunk, wasting bandwidth/CPU and potentially downloading data that will be rejected anyway": 0.021047161892056465, "The new auto-downsize loop doesn't check whether downsizing succeeded and doesn't enforce that the final file is under max_image_size_kb before proceeding, which can cause repeated expensive processing and still fail uploads": 0.9156928062438965, "The downsize loop always uses allow_animated_thumbnails, which can strip animation for avatar uploads even when allow_animated_avatars is enabled": 0.7779346704483032}